From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CEB-GNRD board layer <bmc@localhost>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: show the update progress and the current step

Show a progress bar under the update form: the upload percentage, then the
PercentComplete of the Redfish update task that bmcweb returns, polled every
2 s.  The package MANIFEST tells a BIOS update from a BMC update.  For the BIOS
the step is named from the progress value that the board's bios-update.sh
reports (waiting for the server to be off, switching the flash, erasing,
writing, verifying, returning the flash, force-off pulse, power-on), and the
page reports success or the step that failed.  A BMC update still ends with
the BMC reboot and the refresh reminder.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD board-specific update flow]
